 comorb:["Obesity, heart failure, arthritis limiting mobility, lymphoedema, cellulitis"],
 signs:["Aching heavy legs worse at end of day, oedema, varicosities, haemosiderin staining (brown), venous eczema, lipodermatosclerosis (inverted champagne bottle), atrophie blanche","Ulcer: shallow, irregular, wet, sloughy base, gaiter area, moderate pain, pulses present"],
 red:["Sudden increase in pain, spreading redness, fever: cellulitis or infected ulcer","Ulcer with absent pulses, punched-out, on the toes or heel: arterial, not venous, no compression","Ulcer not healing in 12 weeks or changing shape: biopsy for malignancy"],
 compl:["Chronic ulceration, cellulitis, contact dermatitis from dressings, reduced mobility"],
 nurse:["ABPI first (compression safe at 0.8–1.3), then graduated compression is the treatment: bandaging or stockings","Elevation above heart level, calf exercises, walking, weight, skin care with emollient","Wound: measure and photograph, manage exudate, watch for infection; healed ulcers need lifelong compression"],
