 signs:["Breathless on exertion (mMRC grade), chronic cough, sputum, wheeze, barrel chest, pursed-lip breathing, tripod posture, reduced breath sounds, prolonged expiration","Exacerbation: more breathless, more sputum, sputum colour change, more wheeze, more reliever use"],
 red:["Cannot complete a sentence, RR over 25, HR over 110, SpO₂ below their target (usually 88–92%), drowsy or confused (CO₂ retention), cyanosis, silent chest: 000","Chest pain or new oedema with an exacerbation (PE, heart failure, pneumothorax)"],
 compl:["Respiratory failure, cor pulmonale, pneumothorax, pneumonia, lung cancer, frailty and cachexia"],
